{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-58758","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-113414","text":"R0.4.3 custody & provenance model — written before the mechanism"}]},{"id":"blk-58759","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113415","text":"Two invariants discovered by the R0.4.2 review:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58761","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113416","marks":["bold"],"text":"Replay may reconstruct knowledge; replay alone must never reconstruct possession."}]}],"id":"blk-58760","kind":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58763","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113417","marks":["bold"],"text":"Naming something cannot grant lifecycle authority over it."}]}],"id":"blk-58762","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-58764","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-113418","text":"Knowledge vs possession"}]},{"id":"blk-58765","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113419","marks":["code"],"text":"replay_lifecycle(log)"},{"id":"spn-113420","text":" answers \"what is believed about locus L\" — it is public, descriptive, and mints nothing. Acting "},{"id":"spn-113421","marks":["italic"],"text":"as"},{"id":"spn-113422","text":" a participant requires a possession value that public evidence cannot produce:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-58767","spans":[{"id":"spn-113423","text":"To act as…"}]},{"id":"blk-58768","spans":[{"id":"spn-113424","text":"You must hold…"}]}],"id":"blk-58766","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-58769","spans":[{"id":"spn-113425","text":"the live Carrier"}]},{"id":"blk-58770","spans":[{"id":"spn-113426","marks":["code"],"text":"LocusAttachment"},{"id":"spn-113427","text":" (live) or "},{"id":"spn-113428","marks":["code"],"text":"CarrierCustody"},{"id":"spn-113429","text":" (persisted recovery material) + the log"}]}],[{"id":"blk-58771","spans":[{"id":"spn-113430","text":"the finality authority"}]},{"id":"blk-58772","spans":[{"id":"spn-113431","marks":["code"],"text":"FinalityWarden"}]}],[{"id":"blk-58773","spans":[{"id":"spn-113432","text":"a lifecycle creator"}]},{"id":"blk-58774","spans":[{"id":"spn-113433","marks":["code"],"text":"WorldRoot"},{"id":"spn-113434","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-113435","marks":["code"],"text":"LocusRoot"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-58775","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-113436","text":"Provenance chain"}]},{"id":"blk-58776","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"WorldRoot::bootstrap(mark)          <- THE trust boundary (see below)\n   │  create_locus(LocusId)\n   ▼\nLocusRoot                            (move-only; one lifecycle start each)\n   │  begin()\n   ▼\nVacantLocus(0) + FinalityWarden\n   │  attach(carrier)\n   ▼\nLocusAttachment(N) ── suspend() ──> CarrierCustody(N)   [CONSUMES the live value]\nCarrierCustody(N)  ── recover_attachment(custody, &admission) ──> LocusAttachment(N)   [admission = current, linear]"},{"id":"blk-58777","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113437","text":"(R0.4.5: Live XOR Recoverable. The former "},{"id":"spn-113438","marks":["code"],"text":"custody()"},{"id":"spn-113439","text":" accessor was removed because it aliased live and recoverable possession.) Every minted value and evidence record privately carries the root's "},{"id":"spn-113440","marks":["code"],"text":"mark"},{"id":"spn-113441","text":". A "},{"id":"spn-113442","marks":["code"],"text":"LocusId"},{"id":"spn-113443","text":" appears nowhere in this chain as an input that grants anything: knowing a name mints no vacancy, no warden, no custody."}]},{"id":"blk-58778","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-113444","text":"Recovery model (review cases A–D)"}]},{"id":"blk-58779","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58781","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113445","text":"**A. Same-Carrier planned restart (linear checkpointed"}]}],"id":"blk-58780","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58782","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113446","text":"reconstitution):** "},{"id":"spn-113447","marks":["code"],"text":"suspend()"},{"id":"spn-113448","text":" consumes the live attachment and yields the one "},{"id":"spn-113449","marks":["code"],"text":"CarrierCustody"},{"id":"spn-113450","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-113451","marks":["code"],"text":"recover_attachment(custody, &admission)"},{"id":"spn-113452","text":" consumes the custody and yields the live attachment again, judged against the lineage's CURRENT "},{"id":"spn-113453","marks":["code"],"text":"LifecycleAdmission"},{"id":"spn-113454","text":" (R0.4.6/7 — never a caller-chosen slice; see docs/freshness-model.md, docs/admission-model.md). Recovery never advances a generation; a failed recovery hands the custody back. This is planned restart only — see docs/linearity-model.md for why unplanned crash recovery is NOT claimed."}]},{"id":"blk-58783","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58785","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113455","marks":["bold"],"text":"B. Physical Carrier loss:"},{"id":"spn-113456","text":" the custody material died with the"}]}],"id":"blk-58784","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58786","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113457","text":"Carrier. Orderly detach is therefore "},{"id":"spn-113458","marks":["italic"],"text":"unavailable"},{"id":"spn-113459","text":" — exactly as intended — and only the warden's finality path can close the generation."}]},{"id":"blk-58787","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58789","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113460","marks":["bold"],"text":"C. Network partition:"},{"id":"spn-113461","text":" the log stays readable everywhere, but a"}]}],"id":"blk-58788","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58790","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113462","text":"reader holds neither A's custody nor a finality decision. The generation stays attached to A. Knowledge without possession."}]},{"id":"blk-58791","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58793","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113463","marks":["bold"],"text":"D. Vacant locus:"},{"id":"spn-113464","text":" passive knowledge of vacancy is NOT mutation"}]}],"id":"blk-58792","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58794","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113465","text":"authority (explicit decision). A "},{"id":"spn-113466","marks":["code"],"text":"VacantLocus"},{"id":"spn-113467","text":" value is held only by (i) the releasing Carrier via "},{"id":"spn-113468","marks":["code"],"text":"detach(admission)"},{"id":"spn-113469","text":" (which may hand it off deliberately), or (ii) the finality authority via "},{"id":"spn-113470","marks":["code"],"text":"finalize_loss(…, admission)"},{"id":"spn-113471","text":", which materializes the successor vacancy atomically with the closure (R0.4.7)."}]},{"id":"blk-58795","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-113472","text":"Two-layer provenance checking"}]},{"id":"blk-58796","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58798","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113473","marks":["code"],"text":"replay_lifecycle"},{"id":"spn-113474","text":" (public, descriptive) additionally rejects logs"}]}],"id":"blk-58797","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-58799","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113475","text":"whose events carry differing marks ("},{"id":"spn-113476","marks":["code"],"text":"MixedProvenance"},{"id":"spn-113477","text":"): splicing forged-root evidence into an honest history fails even descriptively."}]},{"id":"blk-58800","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58802","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113478","marks":["code"],"text":"audit_replay(&WorldRoot, …)"},{"id":"spn-113479","text":" (authoritative, descriptive) verifies"}]}],"id":"blk-58801","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-58803","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113480","text":"every event against the root's own mark ("},{"id":"spn-113481","marks":["code"],"text":"ForeignProvenance"},{"id":"spn-113482","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-58804","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58806","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113483","marks":["code"],"text":"LifecycleAdmission"},{"id":"spn-113484","text":" (linear, current) is bound to the lineage mark"}]}],"id":"blk-58805","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-58807","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113485","text":"from birth; every transition checks the acting value's provenance against it ("},{"id":"spn-113486","marks":["code"],"text":"ForeignProvenance"},{"id":"spn-113487","text":") and hands everything back on failure."}]},{"id":"blk-58808","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-113488","text":"The trust boundary, stated exactly (no papering over)"}]},{"id":"blk-58809","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113489","marks":["code"],"text":"WorldRoot::bootstrap(mark)"},{"id":"spn-113490","text":" is publicly callable — a library cannot make a global singleton. What the types DO enforce, in-process: no API reveals a mark (no accessor, no PartialEq on custody), so a holder of records, logs, custody-less state, or LocusIds cannot extract or forge the mark; evidence minted under a different bootstrap is rejected by both layers above. What is NOT claimed: cryptographic attestation (marks are modeling material, not crypto — skepticism list unchanged), secrecy of the bootstrap entropy (a deployment duty), or cross-log split-brain resolution. The claim is narrowed to exactly this: "},{"id":"spn-113491","marks":["bold"],"text":"within a process, neither public evidence nor a LocusId can manufacture custody or finality capability; only material descending from the same bootstrap can."}]},{"id":"blk-58810","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-113492","text":"Falsifiers this model must survive (implemented in R0.4.3)"}]},{"id":"blk-58811","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58813","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113493","text":"Honest "},{"id":"spn-113494","marks":["code"],"text":"Attached(A,0)"},{"id":"spn-113495","text":" log + no A-local custody → no way to mint"}]}],"id":"blk-58812","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-58814","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113496","marks":["code"],"text":"DetachReceipt(A,0)"},{"id":"spn-113497","text":" (Attack A dead; "},{"id":"spn-113498","marks":["code"],"text":"reconstitute"},{"id":"spn-113499","text":" no longer exists)."}]},{"id":"blk-58815","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58817","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113500","marks":["code"],"text":"VacantLocus::genesis"},{"id":"spn-113501","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-113502","marks":["code"],"text":"genesis_with_warden"},{"id":"spn-113503","text":" no longer exist —"}]}],"id":"blk-58816","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-58818","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113504","text":"LocusId-based minting is a compile error."}]},{"id":"blk-58819","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58821","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113505","text":"A forged-root warden's finalization spliced into an honest log →"}]}],"id":"blk-58820","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-58822","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113506","marks":["code"],"text":"MixedProvenance"},{"id":"spn-113507","text":"; a fully forged log → "},{"id":"spn-113508","marks":["code"],"text":"ForeignProvenance"},{"id":"spn-113509","text":" on audit."}]},{"id":"blk-58823","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58825","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113510","text":"Direct struct construction of custody/warden/records still E0451."}]}],"id":"blk-58824","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58827","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113511","text":"Stale custody (from a closed generation) cannot recover."}]}],"id":"blk-58826","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58829","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113512","text":"Custody for the wrong carrier cannot recover."}]}],"id":"blk-58828","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58831","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-113513","text":"Legitimate bootstrap still creates and runs a full lifecycle."}]}],"id":"blk-58830","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieracomhodbae3ji4gg6jnag5jph2c6po752gymnwatkapurifrir6dq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}